mox on FenrirOS
===============

mox is a complete mail server in one program (SMTP, IMAP, webmail, SPF,
DKIM, DMARC, MTA-STS, DANE, junk filtering, ACME). Nothing is configured or
running after installation: no configuration, no accounts, no keys.

Layout: the program is /usr/bin/mox; its working directory is /var/lib/mox
(config/ and data/ below it, made by quickstart). The system user is _mox.

1. As root, in /var/lib/mox, generate the configuration, an account, its
   password and DKIM keys, passing the user mox should run as:
       cd /var/lib/mox
       mox quickstart you@example.org _mox
   (add -existing-webserver when nginx or another server already has ports
   80/443). Read quickstart.log: it lists the DNS records to create.
2. Check the result: mox -config /var/lib/mox/config/mox.conf config test
3. Start it: dinitctl enable mox
   (the service runs "mox -config /var/lib/mox/config/mox.conf serve").
   quickstart's mox.service is for systemd; ignore it.
4. Admin web interface: http://localhost/admin/ (the password quickstart
   printed). More: https://www.xmox.nl/
